[{:seon.task/name "ns-keeps-its-metadata"
  :seon.task/plan "Jolt's `(ns ^:scratch foo)` attaches no metadata to the namespace, so a namespace cannot be declared ^:scratch from the REPL (`seon.program/scratch-ns?` reads `(:scratch (meta nsx))`). Two stopgaps stand in: `seon.agent/make-ns!` sets it with `alter-meta!` (src/seon/agent.clj:446) and `seon.program/recording` reapplies the ns form's metadata (`ns-meta`). On the JVM, `(meta (find-ns 'foo))` holds the ns form's metadata. Cause: Jolt's ns macro (host/chez/ns.ss). Correct, on a `jolt/<topic>` branch: the ns form's metadata (docstring and attr-map too) merges onto the namespace. Deletes both stopgaps (every definition happens once)."
  :seon.task/kind :work
  :seon.task/proofs #{seon.program-test/a-scratch-ns-declared-at-the-repl-stays-scratch}}
 {:seon.task/name "whole-program-inference-keeps-nil-checks"
  :seon.task/plan "Done (Jolt be2495af, `jolt/infer-nil-union`, in the pin). Reproduction: in a built binary, `seon.ref/line-citation` threw `parse-long requires a string` for `src/a.clj:50` (it destructures `[from to]` and tests `(or (nil? to) (parse-long to))`), so a built root could not load a task file citing `path:N`. Cause, in Jolt's intra-procedural inference (not the whole-program pass): `jolt.passes.types/infer-call` typed an element read (`nth`, `first`, `second`, `peek`, `last`, `fnext`) off a typed vector as the element, and `jolt.passes.types/pred-on` folds `nil?` false on a concrete scalar; destructuring reads `(nth v 1 nil)`. Now the read joins the element with the default (`nth`'s 3-arity) or `:nil`; Jolt's build-smoke elem-nil case proves it."
  :seon.task/kind :work
  :seon.task/proofs #{seon.root-test/a-built-root-reads-a-line-citation}}
 {:seon.task/name "a-build-without-whole-program-inference-compiles-tools-reader"
  :seon.task/plan "Done (Jolt d7ec259b, `jolt/eval-outside-build`, in the pin). Reproduction: `JOLT_NO_WP_INFER=1 bin/build seon` failed with `variable jv$clojure.tools.reader.impl.utils/<=clojure-1-7-alpha5 is not bound` (tools.reader's `compile-when`); smallest case test/build/build/reader.clj. Cause: the build publishes a compilation unit with direct-linking on and registers each emitted def in it (jolt-core/jolt/backend_scheme.clj, `direct-linkable?`), and `compile-when` evals at expansion (host/chez/compile-eval.ss `jolt-analyze-emit-form`) against that unit, so it linked a jv$ that exists only in emitted text; whole-program inference expanded every macro before any def was emitted, which hid it. Now the build records the process's unit (`ce-build-unit-enter!`) and the process's own analyze-and-eval compiles against it with optimize and direct-linking off (`ce-outside-build`); build-smoke's eval-at-expansion case builds with inference on and off. Note: Jolt reads the switch with `getenv`, so an empty `JOLT_NO_WP_INFER=` also turns inference off."
  :seon.task/kind :work
  :seon.task/proofs #{seon.root-test/a-build-without-whole-program-inference-reads-with-tools-reader}}]
